ogy and biology of <italic>Sanmiguelia lewisii</italic>, and its bearing on angiosperm evolution in the late Triassic</article-title><source>Evol Trends Plant</source><year>1989</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>25</fpage><lpage>51</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Friis</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name><name><surname>Doyle</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Endress</surname><given-names>PK</given-names></name><name><surname>Leng</surname><given-names>Q</given-names></name></person-group><article-title><italic>Archaefructus </italic>&#x02013; angiosperm precursor or specialized early angiosperm?</article-title><source>Trends Plant Sci</source><year>2003</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>369</fpage><lpage>373</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12927969</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S1360-1385(03)00161-4</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pan</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The Jurassic precursors of angiosperms from Yanliao region of North China and the origin of angiosperms</article-title><source>Chin Sci Bull</source><year>1983</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>15</fpage><lpage>20</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pan</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Juglandaceous plant (<italic>Pterocarya</italic>) from middle Jurassic of Yanliao region, north China</article-title><source>Acta Sci Nat Univ Sunyatseni</source><year>1997</year><volume>36</volume><fpage>80</fpage><lpage>86</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pan</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Rhamnaceous plants from middle Jurassic of Yanliao region, north China</article-title><source>Bull Geol Soc Liaoning Prov, China</source><year>1990</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>8</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Xu</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Do fossil angiosperms really occur in Jurassic beds of the Yanshan-Liaoning area, north China</article-title><source>Chin Sci Bull</source><year>1987</year><volume>32</volume><fpage>1712</fpage><lpage>1714</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kimura</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Ohana</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Zhao</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name><name><surname>Geng</surname><given-names>BY</given-names></name></person-group><article-title><italic>Pankuangia haifanggouensis </italic>gen. et sp. nov., a fossil plant with unknown affinity from the middle Jurassic Haifanggou Fromation, western Liaoning, Northeast China</article-title><source>Bull Kitakyushu Mus Nat Hist</source><year>1994</year><volume>13</volume><fpage>255</fpage><lpage>261</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="B20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ji</surname><given-names>Q</given-names></name><name><surname>Li</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Bowe</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Taylor</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Early Cretaceous <italic>Archaefructus eoflora </italic>sp. nov. with bisexual flowers from Beipiao, Western Liaoning, China</article-title><source>Acta Geol Sin</source><year>2004</year><volume>78</volume><fpage>883